<title>ITALY: Italy cabinet did not discuss Stet sale - minister.</title>
<headline>Italy cabinet did not discuss Stet sale - minister.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian cabinet did not discuss the privatisation of state telecommunications holding Stet at its meeting on Friday morning, Civil Service Minister Franco Bassanini told reporters.</p>
<p>The cabinet had been expected to approve a decree setting out guidelines for the sell-off which the government hopes to carry out by mid-October.</p>
<p>Stet managing director Tomaso Tommasi di Vignano had said on Wednesday he expected the decree to go to the cabinet this week.</p>
<p>--Rome bureau +39 66782501</p>
